  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">P&#xe1;tria Amaz&#xf4;nia Credit Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project consists of an investment of up to R$200 million (approximately US$35 million) in P&#xe1;tria Cr&#xe9;dito Amaz&#xf4;nia (the &#x201c;Fund&#x201d;), which will aim to build a portfolio of structured debt investments to support companies operating in the Legal Amaz&#xf4;nia. The Fund will be managed by P&#xe1;tria Investimentos (the &#x201c;Fund Manager&#x201d; or &#x201c;P&#xe1;tria&#x201d;).With a target size of R$1 billion (approximately US$175 million), the Fund is expected to make approximately 20 investments with ticket sizes typically ranging from R$50 million to R$100 million (approximately US$9 million to US$18 million) throughout its life. The Fund will focus on sustainable industrial development, sustainable agriculture, transportation efficiency, logistics and warehousing projects, and financial inclusion. The Fund will have a nine-year term and a seven-year investment period.</narrative>
  </description>
